    "color": "#0f7a5a",
    "visibility": "public",
    "description_md": "Hydrographic products DERIVED from the CalCOFI CTD cast profiles rather than measured: spice (spiciness at 0 dbar, TEOS-10) and the sensor-pair averaged sigma-theta at every published CTD depth; and, per cast, the mixed-layer depth (the CalCOFI legacy definition, with two alternative criteria beside it), the depth and value of the chlorophyll-a maximum, the chlorophyll-a integrated over the top 200 m, the hypoxic boundary depths (where oxygen falls to 2.4, 1.4 and 0.5 mL/L), the nitracline depth (where nitrate reaches 1 umol/L), the pycnocline depth (the maximum of the TEOS-10 buoyancy frequency N2, also published per depth), by the definitions of the CalCOFI CTD team. Computed from the full-resolution 1 m bins of the CalCOFI CTD Cast Files after the provider's quality flags are applied.\n",
    "keywords": ["EARTH SCIENCE > OCEANS > SALINITY/DENSITY > DENSITY", "EARTH SCIENCE > OCEANS > OCEAN CIRCULATION > OCEAN MIXED LAYER", "EARTH SCIENCE > OCEANS > OCEAN CHEMISTRY > CHLOROPHYLL", "EARTH SCIENCE > OCEANS > OCEAN CHEMISTRY > OXYGEN", "EARTH SCIENCE > OCEANS > OCEAN CHEMISTRY > NITRATE", "EARTH SCIENCE > OCEANS > SALINITY/DENSITY > PYCNOCLINE"],
